\section*{The Crossing Number of the Complete Bipartite Graph}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
\textit{Complete bipartite crossing numbers}: The manuscript claims the Zarankiewicz formula for the ordinary crossing number of $K_{m,n}$ for all positive part sizes. It gives both the lower bound and a drawing realizing the four-floor product.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
\textit{Complete bipartite crossing numbers}: Signed interior intersections are combined with endpoint spoke order to define a cycle-pairing matrix. An interpolation inequality for subspace intersections gives a rank-sum lower bound, while an order detector removes the row and column ambiguities in the drawing data. Off-diagonal ranks are charged to actual crossings, and a balanced-axis drawing supplies equality.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
\textit{Complete bipartite crossing numbers}: The claimed formula covers all positive part sizes m,n and agrees with the brick-factory upper bound; it proves the required lower bound for arbitrary topological drawings.

With the hypotheses and conventions above, the claimed result addresses the whole mathematical assertion on this page.

\subsection{Formal verification}
Family 165 describes Lean coverage for the two exact ordinary crossing formulas and drawings attaining them.

\textit{Complete bipartite crossing numbers}: The manuscript links \texttt{BipartiteCrossing.lean} (declaration \texttt{OAI.Zarankiewicz.mainTarget\_proof}), \texttt{CompleteCrossing.lean} (declaration \texttt{OAI.Paper170.complete\_graph\_crossing\_number}).

The documented selection includes this manuscript’s main assertion; that assertion retains the restrictions stated above.

This site has not run the Lean development. These links describe OpenAI’s selected formal statements and should be read with their stated scope.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI reports that an internal model produced the manuscripts. Their arguments have not been independently verified as proofs by this site. Any portion outside the documented formal scope may contain mistakes, and the catalogue label reports the announced mathematical claim.

